    "body": "Universal developer preview of Roomlet 0.1.0 (build 1), for macOS 15 or later.\nThe ZIP contains the native arm64/x86_64 app, license and preview guide. No\nexternal runtime, account or hosted service is required.\n\nDownload the ZIP with its checksum and manifest, compare SHA-256, then extract\nwith Finder's Archive Utility. ZIP SHA-256:\n`8f24b5f348d4f8955f9ff8b2ceea3a316ba8fff8d96529dcdf2f0546287aedea`.\n\nBoth Release builds, strict signatures, the existing sandbox/user-selected\nread-write entitlements on each architecture, source-exact resources and fresh\nZIP extraction passed in [the bounded packaging run](https://github.com/alvarovillalbaa/roomlet/actions/runs/42474856669).\nThe app was built from `ee3b98772e150b6c8e9c332954705ee3a49b9ecd`; the release\ntag adds preserved results and distribution records without changing checked\napp/build inputs. The first failed observer attempt remains documented.\n\nThis is an ad-hoc signed developer preview without Developer ID or notarization.\nGatekeeper/fresh-Mac installation, native UI, folder selection/security scope,\nscanning, real Trash and reclaimed space remain unverified. If macOS refuses\nthe app, stop and inspect source or wait for trusted distribution. Follow the\nbundled guide with disposable local files; nothing has been checked against\npersonal folders. Moving files to Trash does not reclaim their space.\n\n[Packaging evidence and limits](https://github.com/alvarovillalbaa/roomlet/blob/v0.1.0-preview.1/docs/results/2026/11-08/preview-package-attempt-2.md)\nand [source](https://github.com/alvarovillalbaa/roomlet).\n"
  },
